ic quantization of gravity from the null cone"},"url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.34924"}},"_tags":["story","author_hecmmm","story_50651863","front_page"],"author":"hecmmm","children":[50651864,50653101,50653870,50654725,50655267,50655340,50655666,50655738,50655788,50655863,50656019,50657129,50657961,50658352,50658488,50658959,50660680,50660839,50661590,50662701,50665309],"created_at":"2026-11-26T05:37:51Z","created_at_i":1795671471,"num_comments":99,"objectID":"50651863","points":250,"story_id":50651863,"title":"An algebraic quantization of gravity from the null cone","updated_at":"2026-11-27T13:17:47Z","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.34924"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"thanato0s"},"story_text":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"I'm glad to announce that I'm releasing my new book, Learning to Play Vim.<p>When I started using Vim more than a decade ago, I wished there was a manual out there teaching how to use this fantastic editor step by step, beginning with the foundations up to more advanced features. Of course at the time I did the vimtutor, but it was too dense for me to remember much from it. I also read the entire Vim manual (`:help manual`), but I didn't like it: it was too detailed in places (for example `02.8 Finding help` completely lost me for a while), and other features didn't get the treatment they deserved.<p>So I decided to write my own Vim manual. It took me more than 4 years and 2987 focused pomodoros (1244 hours) of work to finally get it done!<p>The result:<p>- 21 chapters showing the most important Vim features step by step.<p>- 170 exercises with solutions.<p>- Many real-life examples to show how Vim can be used and configured for your own needs.<p>- The related Vim's help pages to dig further into each feature.<p>Most configs are both written in Vimscript and Lua for Neovim users. This book explores the common features between Vim and Neovim, so don't expect anything about Neovim-specific features (like treesitter or LSP for example).<p>- The landing page: <a href=\"https://themouseless.dev/vim/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://themouseless.dev/vim/</a><p>- A sample of the book with the entire table of contents and the first three chapters covering most of the basics: <a href=\"https://themouseless.dev/content/learning_to_play_vim_sample.pdf\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://themouseless.dev/content/learning_to_play_vim_sample...</a>.<p>I wrote this with my bare hands, no LLM involved to spoil the fun."},"title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Show HN: I wrote an entire Vim manual over 4 years"},"url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"http://themouseless.dev/vim/"}},"_tags":["story","author_thanato0s","story_50655868","show_hn","front_page"],"author":"thanato0s","children":[50659031,50659060,50659197,50659635,50660378,50660592,50661419,50661447,50661678,50662782,50662998,50663102,50663721,50663937,50663968,50664458,50665710],"created_at":"2026-11-26T14:44:22Z","created_at_i":1795704262,"num_comments":69,"objectID":"50655868","points":226,"story_id":50655868,"story_text":"I&#x27;m glad to announce that I&#x27;m releasing my new book, Learning to Play Vim.<p>When I started using Vim more than a decade ago, I wished there was a manual out there teaching how to use this fantastic editor step by step, beginning with the foundations up to more advanced features. Of course at the time I did the vimtutor, but it was too dense for me to remember much from it. I also read the entire Vim manual (`:help manual`), but I didn&#x27;t like it: it was too detailed in places (for example `02.8 Finding help` completely lost me for a while), and other features didn&#x27;t get the treatment they deserved.<p>So I decided to write my own Vim manual. It took me more than 4 years and 2987 focused pomodoros (1244 hours) of work to finally get it done!<p>The result:<p>- 21 chapters showing the most important Vim features step by step.<p>- 170 exercises with solutions.<p>- Many real-life examples to show how Vim can be used and configured for your own needs.<p>- The related Vim&#x27;s help pages to dig further into each feature.<p>Most configs are both written in Vimscript and Lua for Neovim users. This book explores the common features between Vim and Neovim, so don&#x27;t expect anything about Neovim-specific features (like treesitter or LSP for example).<p>- The landing page: <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;themouseless.dev&#x2F;vim&#x2F;\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;themouseless.dev&#x2F;vim&#x2F;</a><p>- A sample of the book with the entire table of contents and the first three chapters covering most of the basics: <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;themouseless.dev&#x2F;content&#x2F;learning_to_play_vim_sample.pdf\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;themouseless.dev&#x2F;content&#x2F;learning_to_play_vim_sample...</a>.<p>I wrote this with my bare hands, no LLM involved to spoil the fun.","title":"Show HN: I wrote an entire Vim manual over 4 years","updated_at":"2026-11-27T13:17:47Z","url":"http://themouseless.dev/vim/"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"todsacerdoti"},"title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"The need for a formally verifiable mainstream programming language"},"url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"https://blainehansen.me/post/mainstream-verifiable-language/"}},"_tags":["story","author_todsacerdoti","story_50663089","front_page"],"author":"todsacerdoti","children":[50663245,50663382,50663473,50663486,50663491,50663494,50663517,50663544,50663552,50663571,50663578,50663599,50663609,50663619,50663627,50663653,50663661,50663676,50663678,50663680,50663684,50663727,50663754,50663761,50663784,50663788,50663802,50663857,50663886,50663893,50663903,50663928,50663944,50664004,50664041,50664085,50664100,50664137,50664139,50664170,50664199,50664230,50664236,50664250,50664252,50664256,